From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [core,nla] accept TSRemoteGuardCreds without
 supplementalCreds

supplementalCreds in TSRemoteGuardCreds is OPTIONAL ([MS-CSSP]
2.2.1.2.3), and FreeRDP's own client never sends it
(nla_encode_ts_remoteguard_credentials). When it is absent it is also
the last element, so WinPrAsn1DecReadContextualSequence() finds nothing
to read and reports an error, and nla_read_ts_credentials() rejects the
credentials with "invalid supplementalCreds": a server with Remote
Credential Guard enabled refused every FreeRDP client using /remoteGuard.

Peek at the next tag first, as set_creds_octetstring_to_settings() does
for the optional TSSmartCardCreds fields, and read supplementalCreds
only when it is there.
---
 libfreerdp/core/nla.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfreerdp/core/nla.c b/libfreerdp/core/nla.c
index 78232ed..cf2b961 100644
--- a/libfreerdp/core/nla.c
+++ b/libfreerdp/core/nla.c
@@ -1563,8 +1563,16 @@ static BOOL nla_read_ts_credentials(rdpNla* nla, SecBuffer* data)
 			MSV1_0_REMOTE_SUPPLEMENTAL_CREDENTIAL* suppCreds = nullptr;
 			WinPrAsn1Decoder suppCredsSeq = WinPrAsn1Decoder_init();
 
-			if (WinPrAsn1DecReadContextualSequence(&dec2, 1, &error, &suppCredsSeq) &&
-			    Stream_GetRemainingLength(&suppCredsSeq.source))
+			/* Absent (the FreeRDP client never sends it): nothing left to read, which
+			 * WinPrAsn1DecReadContextualSequence() reports as an error. */
+			WinPrAsn1_tag suppCredsTag = 0;
+			if (!WinPrAsn1DecPeekTag(&dec2, &suppCredsTag) ||
+			    (suppCredsTag != (ER_TAG_CONTEXTUAL | 1)))
+			{
+				/* no supplementalCreds */
+			}
+			else if (WinPrAsn1DecReadContextualSequence(&dec2, 1, &error, &suppCredsSeq) &&
+			         Stream_GetRemainingLength(&suppCredsSeq.source))
 			{
 				WinPrAsn1Decoder ntlmCredsSeq = WinPrAsn1Decoder_init();
 				if (!WinPrAsn1DecReadSequence(&suppCredsSeq, &ntlmCredsSeq))
